  "result": "Excellent! The customer tier discounts feature is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Customer Tier Discounts Implementation\n\n### Key Changes:\n\n1. **`src/customers.js`** \u2014 Exported `TIER_DISCOUNTS` constant:\n   ```javascript\n   export const TIER_DISCOUNTS = {\n     gold: 5,      // 5% discount\n     silver: 2.5,  // 2.5% discount\n     standard: 0,  // No discount\n   };\n   ```\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** \u2014 Updated `createInvoice` to apply tier discounts:\n   - When `discountPercent` is **undefined**, applies the customer's tier discount\n   - When `discountPercent` is **defined** (including 0), uses that value instead (tier discount is overridden)\n   - This distinction is important: `0` = explicit no discount, `undefined` = use tier default\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 10 comprehensive test cases covering:\n   - Gold/silver/standard tier discounts applied correctly\n   - Explicit discountPercent (0 and non-zero) overriding tier discounts\n   - Multiple lines with mixed tier and explicit discounts\n   - Totals calculations with tier-based discounts\n   - Updated existing render tests to use standard-tier customers for predictable amounts\n\n**All 89 tests pass** (79 previous + 10 new tier discount tests). The implementation:\n- Keeps tier percentages in one place (TIER_DISCOUNTS)\n- Never mutates arguments\n- Uses integer cents throughout\n- Properly rounds fractional amounts\n- Clamps all values to 0 minimum",
